{"author":{"id":"836d943203cf5a4f01ab5d4b4780de84949c43734f2256a167cc5931ae5d8c66"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1794172917,"nonce":"7R3Q4UeM2b93VNwOvMJbEIIKX/s=","target":"569cbe248e5bf942681a8da679b9f487d9fc040043f5b6f1d54e37e264f35415","message":"## Context\n`App` (`src/main.rs:48`) holds only theme and section; the top bar's Repositories pill and sync pill (`src/ui/screen.rs:44`) do nothing. The app must never freeze and always show what is loading.\n\n## Files\n- `src/main.rs:48` `App`, `:67` `Message`, `:74` `update` — workspace, repos, per-repo load state, async orchestration, subscription\n- `src/ui/screen.rs` — new Repositories page; sidebar header shows the workspace, not one repo; sync pill shows live status\n- `src/ui/components.rs` — new `skeleton` (placeholder card/row) and `spinner_dot`\n\n## Approach\n- `cargo add rfd` (async `AsyncFileDialog`) for the folder picker.\n- Rule: `update` and `view` never do I/O; every git/git-bug/fs call goes through `Task::perform` / `Task::future`.\n- Boot = stale-while-revalidate: `load_snapshot()` (L2) renders cached repos + issues at once, marked stale; then background `discover` → `fingerprint` per repo → `gitbug::list` only for repos whose fingerprint changed, one task per repo (`Task::batch`), concurrency bounded. Write the snapshot back after each repo loads.\n- Per-repo `LoadState`: `Cached`, `Loading`, `Refreshing`, `Ready(n)`, `NoGitBug`, `Locked`, `Error(msg)` — dot via `components::dot` (`src/ui/components.rs:75`) and `Tone`; skeleton cards while nothing is cached yet.\n- Sync pill: \"Loading 3/12…\" while refreshing, \"Synced \u003ctime\u003e\" when idle, error tone when any repo failed.\n- Tracking: `iced::time::every(5s)` subscription re-fingerprints ready repos and reloads only changed ones; skipped while a refresh is in flight. Window refocus triggers the same check.\n- Page: roots list (Add project, Add folder to scan, Remove), discovered repos with status + issue counts, Rescan. Persist every change; persist the theme toggle (`dark`).\n- Leave the mock Epics page as is (L5 replaces it).\n\n## Depends on\nL2 — `Workspace`, `discover`, cache\n\n## Out of scope\n- Issue browsing (L4), writes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Unit test: boot with a snapshot puts repos in `Cached` state before any load result arrives; repo-loaded messages move them to `Ready`; a `Locked` result does not drop other repos\n- Unit test: an unchanged fingerprint produces no `gitbug::list` task\n- No `std::process`, `std::fs` or `.await`-free blocking calls in `update`/`view` (review check)\n- Manual: with 10+ repos the window stays responsive during a full rescan; adding a folder via the picker persists to `workspace.json` and survives restart\n- All three gates pass","files":null}]}